---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PromoUpdateStatus from '../../components/PromoUpdateStatus.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site.mjs';
import { promoStatus } from '../../data/promo-status.mjs';

const title = 'Warfare 1942 Promo Codes & Current Status';
const description = 'Check the current Warfare 1942 promo code status, verification method, version compatibility, and what to inspect before trusting a code list.';
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Are there any working Warfare 1942 promo codes?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: `No active Warfare 1942 promo code has been independently verified for the web or current Android version as of ${promoStatus.lastChecked.label}.`
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: 'Where do I redeem a Warfare 1942 promo code?',
      acceptedAnswer: {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        text: 'A stable redemption menu has not been independently documented across the current Warfare 1942 versions, so version-less redemption instructions should be treated as unverified.'
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/promo-codes/" schema={schema}>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Promo Codes', href: '/promo-codes/' }]} />
      <span class="eyebrow">Code intelligence</span>
      <h1>Warfare 1942 Promo Codes &amp; Current Status</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lede">A code belongs on this page only after its source, platform, reward, and test result can be recorded. Empty space is better than a fabricated reward.</p>
      <p class="page-hero__lede">If you searched for the “Wardogs key,” that is the published <a href="/how-to-play/">keyboard control answer</a>, not a promo code.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <PromoUpdateStatus />
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Version-specific answer</span>
        <h2>Code status by Warfare 1942 version</h2>
        <p>Last checked <time datetime={promoStatus.lastChecked.iso}>{promoStatus.lastChecked.shortLabel}</time>. A result for one build does not automatically apply to another.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-grid">
        <article class="content-card"><span class="eyebrow">Web build</span><h3>No verified active codes</h3><p>No stable redemption field or successful code result has been independently documented in the distributed browser build.</p></article>
        <article class="content-card"><span class="eyebrow">Current Android</span><h3>No verified active codes</h3><p>No code has been independently verified for the current Mosaic Games LLC listing with package <code>com.warfare.ww2.online</code>.</p></article>
        <article class="content-card"><span class="eyebrow">Compatibility</span><h3>Cross-version use is unknown</h3><p>Do not assume web and Android accounts, events, rewards, or redemption systems are shared.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--surface">
    <div class="shell content-grid">
      <article class="content-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">01 · Source</span>
        <h2>Where a code must come from</h2>
        <p>We look for a developer announcement, an in-game event, or another direct source. A search result title or an unsourced list is not enough.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="content-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">02 · Test</span>
        <h2>What must be recorded</h2>
        <p>A publishable result needs the exact code, reward, applicable version, test date, redemption location, and a clear success or failure result.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="content-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">03 · Status</span>
        <h2>How updates work</h2>
        <p>Active, unverified, and expired are separate states. The visible date changes only after the evidence is checked again.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Redemption check</span>
      <h2>No verified redemption steps yet</h2>
      <p>We have not independently documented a stable code-redemption menu for every Warfare 1942 version. For that reason, this page does not publish guessed menu paths such as “Settings → Gift Code.” If the current build exposes a code field, its exact location and platform still need a recorded test.</p>
      <div class="callout">The web build and Android app may not share accounts, events, rewards, or code systems. Treat a version-less code claim as unverified.</div>
      <p>The phrase “Wardogs key” does not identify a redeemable code on the current evidence. It refers to the web-control binding documented in the <a href="/how-to-play/">how-to-play guide</a>.</p>

      <h2>Why a Warfare 1942 code may fail</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It was issued for a different web or mobile release.</li>
        <li>The event or campaign has ended.</li>
        <li>The code is region-limited, account-limited, or single-use.</li>
        <li>Capitalization or a copied space changed the input.</li>
        <li>The list copied a code from another game without evidence.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What to do next</h2>
      <p>Check the <a href="/download/">version comparison</a> first, then use the <a href={site.crazyGamesUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">current CrazyGames page</a> or the official Android listing for direct announcements. If you have reproducible evidence, send it through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
